# Scheduled work: the database is the schedule, the OS is the executor.
#
# Every line here is a process that attaches, does what is due, and exits. The
# "is anything due?" check is a lock-free MVCC read, so overlapping ticks cost
# nothing and claim disjoint work by construction (DESIGN-SERVICE §2).

# Drain the task queue every minute. Safe to overlap: the claim is one atomic
# UPDATE … WHERE id = (SELECT … LIMIT 1) RETURNING, so two runners never take
# the same row.
* * * * * mpedb queue run /var/lib/mpedb/app.mpedb --lease 300

# Keep a table-set map in step, bounded so one invocation cannot run long.
*/5 * * * * mpedb rretl map run /var/lib/mpedb/app.mpedb mymap --max-secs 60

# Pull from an upstream source on the schedule `mpedb advise` recommended.
# `--emit-cron` prints these lines for you rather than having you guess.
17 * * * * mpedb ingest next /var/lib/mpedb/app.mpedb

# Nothing here needs a daemon, and nothing here needs mpedb-pg: the wire
# protocol is for CLIENTS. Scheduled work attaches the file directly, which is
# the cheaper path anyway.
